[Music]  there was an historic hire in the nfl  this week the washington football team  announced jason wright will be its next  team president  wright a former player and partner at  mckinsey and company is the first  black person to hold that title in nfl  history  at age 38 he's also the youngest wright  joins washington at a tumultuous time  in july more than a dozen former female  employees made allegations of sexual  harassment  against team officials the team also  dropped redskins as its name following  decades of criticism  all of this amid the uncertainty of  playing in the upcoming season  surrounding the pandemic jason wright  joins us this morning from his home  in virginia jason good morning and  congratulations  thank you so much it's a pleasure to be  here with you all right well it's good  to have you um  a lot to talk about here i do want to  start with the latest news though  because your coach ron rivera told the  team on thursday night that he has  cancer  can you talk quickly about how ron is  doing and how that changes your job  moving forward  sure i mean he's doing great um both  physically and psychologically  spiritually and i think you've seen that  and what's come from him he's  he's a rock um you know emotionally um  and he's got such clarity of vision his  message has been look i'm gonna do what  i need to do  and let's keep it moving let's keep it  moving forward and that strength has  spread to the team and the staff  doesn't change anything for me except  that i know i really i already knew we  really need to take care of our people  in a different way  and do culture in a different way and be  people-centric i just needed to jump  into that  quite a bit earlier to take care of our  folks because it's hard for everybody in  the community  jason when you talk about that about  being people-centric and taking over  what we just referenced some of the  incidents that have gone in  gone on within the team how do you go  about  changing a culture that's a huge thing  to undertake  yeah it is a big thing to undertake but  frankly it's something that every  organization needs to do to remain high  performing and gratefully  i've been able to do that over the last  seven to eight years you know with my  former company  helping organizations get on that  journey i think you know fundamentally  it's at the individual level about their  mindsets their behaviors  the incentives around why they do their  work and then  transparency a culture that shines a  light  on the behaviors that we want in a  positive way and shines a light on those  that we don't want in the culture  and help to move it into a positive  direction and we also got to get things  right  very technically in the process and  policy sort of way  and the investigation will very much  help us with that and jason you know  we mentioned the historic nature of your  hiring and i heard that you said you  were happy you landed  in this role at this time why  i guess there's a few things number one  the the opportunity to really  shape things for the future of this  franchise are massive you know we're  getting ready to  establish a new identity that's going to  inform the way  that we you know impact the world the  way that we engage  charitably the way we engage with fans  and design the fan experience and that  is  a massive opportunity with great and to  work with great and talented people at  the club to do that  you know we're navigating a covet season  which is complex  tricky and i'm eager to help us navigate  that um  and there's so much opportunity and down  the road we get to build a new stadium  so there's so much about this  that feels like you really get to put  your imprint on something lasting  that it's an exciting thing to be a part  of  jason michelle miller here you sound so  excited but  i have to ask washington dropped that  historic name  redskins as its nickname after nearly  90 years what type of input will you be  looking for in a new name and  and how soon can we expect to see one  yeah i mean again it's so much more than  a name it's  it's so much more than a logo it's it's  an identity and because it's so  important and because it's going to  inform so many things we need to have an  open collaborative what i've been  calling a community-based process  engaging the fans the ones who really  embody the identity of the club out in  the world  they need to be engaged substantively  and over time we need to engage our  players staff sponsors  and also the leaders in the dmv area  because it needs to represent the dmv i  mean that is the area in which we're  located  um and so it's going to take some time  uh and  uh and i think uh it at the end whether  it's the name that  my friends want or my kids want or  whatever it is everybody should be able  to see  their fingerprints on the process and be  united in  the go forward identity jason i don't  envy the number of things on your plate  uh right now but again we do uh  we do congratulate you and really  appreciate you joining us thanks so much

